# Database Rules

## Prisma Usage
- Prisma Client singleton: `import { db } from "@/lib/db"`
- Never use `new PrismaClient()`
- Migration in development: `npx prisma migrate dev --name <name>`
- Migration in deployment: `npx prisma migrate deploy`
- After schema changes: `npx prisma generate`

## Query Rules
- Define queries as functions under `src/server/`
- Do not write Prisma queries directly inside components
- Use `select` to fetch only needed fields (do not fetch the entire model)
- For related data, prefer nested `select` inside `select` over `include` where possible

## Schema Rules
- Every model must have `id`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` fields
- Use `deletedAt DateTime?` for soft deletes (instead of physical deletion)
- Slug fields must be `@unique`
- Define enums in the Prisma schema; do not redefine them in TypeScript

## Example Query Structure
```ts
// src/server/queries/threads.ts
import { db } from "@/lib/db"

export async function getThreadsByCategory(categorySlug: string, page: number) {
  return db.thread.findMany({
    where: { category: { slug: categorySlug } },
    select: {
      id: true,
      title: true,
      slug: true,
      createdAt: true,
      author: { select: { username: true, avatarUrl: true } },
      _count: { select: { posts: true } },
    },
    orderBy: [{ isPinned: "desc" }, { createdAt: "desc" }],
    skip: (page - 1) * 20,
    take: 20,
  })
}
```
